## Purpose

Make Idea Brief promotion consistently safe without slowing ordinary brainstorming. Tool Shed will
run one adaptive semantic readiness review only when the operator explicitly requests it or when
`ts: prm idea` has no fresh ready result. Promotion continues for `READY` and
`READY-WITH-PRM-GATES`, stops for `NOT-READY`, and carries every named residual gate into PRM.

## Desired Outcome

An operator can brainstorm naturally and promote an idea without remembering a closing checklist.
The review remains bound to the exact Idea Brief identity, revision, body hash, and review-contract
version; deterministic tooling owns freshness and routing while the agent supplies evidence-backed
semantic judgment. Ordinary brainstorming performs only cheap metadata comparison and never runs
semantic review.

## First Useful Boundary

- Exactly two semantic-review triggers: explicit manual review and PRM promotion without a fresh
  ready result.
- Three operator verdicts: `READY`, `READY-WITH-PRM-GATES`, and `NOT-READY`.
- One structured database authority for review results, with generated read-only presentation.
- Lossless transfer of named PRM gates.
- Focused qualification of failure, concurrency, interaction, portability, upgrade, and closed-loop
  behavior.

